        "original_id": "0ce043f3-c4d2-558a-a356-c03d9fe270d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Times Square, Manhattan, New York City, West 45th Street, Central Park\n- Buildings: Bertelsmann Building, 1540 Broadway, 432 Park Avenue, Loew's State Theatre\n- People: Paul S. Mezey\n- Companies: Journeyman Pictures\n\nFacts:\n- Loew's State Theatre in New York City closed on February 19, 1987.\n- The former Loew's State Theatre site is now occupied by the Bertelsmann Building.\n- In 2011, 432 Park Avenue was originally proposed to be 1300 feet tall.\n- 432 Park Avenue later topped out at 1396 feet.\n- The former Bertelsmann Building is now known as 1540 Broadway.\n- 1540 Broadway is a 44-story, 733-foot office tower in Times Square in Manhattan, New York City, at West 45th Street.\n- 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City that overlooks Central Park.\n- Paul S. Mezey is a New York-based independent producer.\n- Paul S. Mezey founded Journeyman Pictures.",
